{
  "_id": "2X4YWcPhSMcjlJGv",
  "name": "Deathless",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/life/heart-shadow-red.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>Whatever governs the closing of wounds has decided, in your case, to be generous. Bones knit while the blow that broke them is still landing, and the slow indignities that wear other bodies down: plague, venom, exhaustion, age itself, find nothing in you willing to yield.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>Regeneration equal to twice your level.<ul><li>Choose spirit, vitality, or void at character creation. That damage type deactivates it.</li></ul></li><li>Immune to all persistent damage, poison, and disease.</li><li>You do not need to eat, drink, or sleep.</li><li>Conditions that would reduce by 1 at the end of your turn are removed instead.</li><li>Choose two damage types. You gain resistance 5 to each, changeable during daily preparations.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Chosen resistances increase to 10.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>7th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Immune to Drained.</li><li>Regeneration increases to three times your level.</li><li>Choose one resistant type and become immune to it.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>9th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Chosen resistances increase to 15.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>11th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Immune to Clumsy and Enfeebled.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>13th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Gain Resist All 5.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>You no longer need to breathe.</li><li>Choose a second type to become immune to.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>17th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Chosen resistances increase to 20.</li><li>Resist All increases to 10.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>19th Level</strong></p><ul><li>You no longer gain the Unconscious condition at 0 Hit Points unless your regeneration is deactivated. You are instead Slowed 1 until you begin a turn above 0 Hit Points.</li></ul>\n<p><em>Your regeneration is deactivated when you take at least 1 point of damage of your chosen type, or from an effect bearing a matching trait. Damage absorbed by temporary Hit Points counts. A missed attack, or a save that reduces the damage to 0, does not. You cannot select your deactivating type as one of your chosen resistances or immunities, and no spell, item, or other effect can grant you resistance or immunity to it. Resist All gained from this talent is the sole exception, and applies to your deactivating type normally.</em></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> choose your deactivating type when you take this talent. Regeneration is offered at the start of each of your turns, and is switched off until the end of your next turn whenever damage of that type, or from an effect with that trait, is applied to you, including damage that temporary Hit Points absorbed. The immunities, the two chosen resistances and Resist All all apply automatically.</p>\n<p>Your two resistances are the <em>Deathless Resistance A</em> and <em>B</em> dropdowns in your effects panel. Set them at daily preparations; do not set either to your deactivating type. The immunities at 7th and 15th ask which type when they arrive.</p>\n<p>For the table: conditions that would reduce by 1 at the end of your turn are removed instead, you need not eat, drink, sleep or (from 15th) breathe, and from 19th you are Slowed 1 rather than Unconscious at 0 Hit Points while your regeneration is active.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
